.SH TYPICAL WORKFLOW

.SS First-time Setup
.EX
$ ./maintain-v7.sh --setup
# Installs all tools, initializes AIDE baseline, configures Fail2Ban
.EE

.SS Weekly Maintenance
.EX
$ ./maintain-v7.sh
# Select Options 3, 4, 5, 6b, 7a in sequence
# OR use Option 15 (Run All Maintenance)
.EE

.SS Monthly Security Audit
.EX
$ ./maintain-v7.sh → Option 12 (Lynis)
# Review hardening index and warnings
.EE

.SS As-Needed Hardening
.EX
$ ./maintain-v7.sh → Options 9-11, 17-21
# Apply individual hardening measures
.EE

.SS Emergency Recovery
.EX
# Boot from USB Recovery Key (created via Option 98)
# Run recover.sh to restore configs or remove hardening
.EE

.SH SAFETY NOTES

.SS AIDE Initialization
First-run AIDE baseline creation may take 3-10 minutes. Network mounts are excluded to prevent hangs.

.SS VirusTotal Free Tier Limits
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
4 file submissions per day (public uploads)
.IP \(bu 2
~4 hash queries per minute
.IP \(bu 2
15-second delay between requests enforced
.RE

.SS GRUB Password
Once set, cannot be removed without:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Option 14 (Revert Hardening) from working system
.IP \(bu 2
Boot from USB Recovery Key and run recover.sh
.RE

.SS AIDE Exclusions (Prevents False Positives)
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
/tmp/.mount_* (AppImage/FUSE mounts)
.IP \(bu 2
/var/log, /run, /dev, /proc, /sys
.IP \(bu 2
Network mounts (/mnt, /media)
.RE

.SH KNOWN ISSUES

.SS debsecan Suite Mismatch
Linux Mint codenames (e.g., "zena") are not recognized by Debian security tracker. Script automatically maps Mint 22.x → Ubuntu "noble" for compatibility.

.SS AIDE Permission Denied on Ephemeral Mounts
GUI applications (Joplin AppImage, etc.) create /tmp/.mount_* paths that AIDE cannot traverse. Already excluded in default config.

.SS VirusTotal API Key Persistence Under sudo
Script resolves home directory correctly when called via sudo using SUDO_USER environment variable.

